{"taskId":"t02","killer":false,"architecture":"b","seed":1001,"startedAt":"2026-08-28T18:16:46.840Z","elapsedMs":263499,"timedOut":false,"runError":null,"finishReason":"finish-tool","packet":{"goal_spec":{"goal":"make the repository's test suite pass, conforming to README.md as the authoritative spec","constraints":["only-src","no-new-deps","api-stable","stay-in-workspace"]},"goal_status":{"phase":"branch-search-complete","hypotheses_investigated":4,"selection":"rank confirmed>inconclusive, then evidence count; selected h1 (confirmed, 4 evidence items)"},"selected_hypothesis":"h1: undefined","verified_facts":["src/keys.js:6 returns `key.trim().toLowerCase()`, lowercasing the key despite README stating 'trim surrounding whitespace only — case is significant'","`node -e \"import('./src/keys.js').then(m=>console.log(JSON.stringify(m.normalizeKey('Alpha'))))\"` printed \"alpha\", not \"Alpha\"","`node --test test/keys.test.js test/cache.test.js` shows exactly the 3 predicted failures: 'keys: case is significant after trim' (actual 'alpha' !== expected 'Alpha'), 'keys: trims surrounding whitespace' (Beta/Gamma lowercased), and 'cache: keys that differ only in case are distinct entries' (get('Alpha') returned 'B' !== 'A', size collapsed to 1)","src/cache.js get/set/has all call normalizeKey, so every cache operation inherits the lowercasing; the trim side works ('cache: surrounding whitespace is trimmed on set and get' passes), isolating the defect to the `.toLowerCase()` call"],"evidence_refs":["branch-report:h1"],"artifact_refs":["src/keys.js","src/cache.js"],"unresolved_questions":["h2: refuted — `src/cache.js` performs its own independent case canonicalization (e.g., lowercasing the key again when keying the internal `entries` Map) separate from `normalizeKey`, so even if `keys.js` were corrected the cache would still merge case-distinct keys. This is a distinct second-layer mechanism that must be ruled out before concluding the defect lives only in `keys.js`.","h3: refuted — The key normalization strips more than surrounding whitespace — e.g., an over-eager regex like `replace(/\\s+/g, '')` or a Unicode-aware trim that also rewrites characters — producing canonical keys that differ from the input beyond case. This is a distinct mechanism from h1 that would also make `normalizeKey('  Beta ')` and `normalizeKey('\\tGamma\\n')` fail, and could additionally corrupt keys containing internal whitespace or non-breaking spaces.","h4: refuted — `src/cache.js` applies asymmetric normalization between the write and read paths — e.g., `set` stores under the normalized key while `get`/`has` look up using the raw (un-normalized) key (or vice versa). Such an asymmetry would reproduce the case test symptom and would also break `cache: surrounding whitespace is trimmed on set and get`; the whitespace test currently passes, which constrains but does not by itself exonerate this mechanism for the case-specific failure."],"recommended_next_action":"Fix the confirmed root cause (src/keys.js, src/cache.js) under src/ per the README spec, then run the test suite to verify."},"telemetry":{"branch":{"phases":[{"phase":"enumerate","ms":69562,"hypotheses":4},{"phase":"investigate","ms":88381,"branches":4,"reportsParsed":4},{"phase":"converge+handoff","ms":157943,"selected":"h1","packetBytes":2930}],"packetBytes":2930,"totalMs":157943,"selectionReason":"rank confirmed>inconclusive, then evidence count; selected h1 (confirmed, 4 evidence items)"},"handoff":{"packetBytes":2930,"packetFields":["goal_spec","goal_status","selected_hypothesis","verified_facts","evidence_refs","artifact_refs","unresolved_questions","recommended_next_action"]},"usage":{"inputTokens":106299,"outputTokens":14146,"cachedTokens":86272,"requests":39,"retries":0,"errors":0}},"verify":{"verdict":"PASS","gates":{"bugNotReproducible":{"ok":true,"exitCode":0,"output":"original bug not reproducible\n"},"trunkTestsPass":{"ok":true,"exitCode":0,"counts":{"tests":8,"pass":8,"fail":0},"tail":"T