0\n# cancelled 0\n# skipped 0\n# todo 0\n# duration_ms 109.2861\n"},"integrity":{"ok":true,"violations":[]},"exports":{"ok":true,"violations":[]}},"constraintsSatisfied":true},"srcFootprint":{"changed":["/src/parse.js"],"added":[],"deleted":[]},"vgcrPass":true,"outputTail":" it. The README requires the parsed priority to be a non-negative integer (radix 10), throwing `RangeError` on invalid input. Because the priority stayed a string, the scheduler's comparator (`compare`) performed lexicographic string ordering instead of numeric ordering, violating the \"interaction rule\" (raw payload strings must never reach the comparator). This caused 4 test failures:\n\n1. `parse: priority is a non-negative integer in the parsed task` — got `'10'` (string) instead of `10`\n2. `parse: throws on non-numeric priority` — no RangeError for `'soon'`\n3. `parse: throws on negative priority` — no RangeError for `'-3'`\n4. `scheduler: lower priority number runs first across digit widths` — `['c','b','a']` (lexicographic: 1, 10, 2) instead of `['c','a','b']` (numeric: 1, 2, 10)\n\n**Fix**: validate the trimmed priority against `/^\\d+$/` (rejects non-digits and negatives), throw `RangeError` on failure, and return `Number.parseInt(trimmed, 10)` as the priority.\n\n**Verification**: `node --test --test-isolation=none` → 8/8 pass.\n\nConstraints: only modified src/parse.js; no dependencies; exported names unchanged; tests untouched; conforms to README; worked only inside the directory.\n","architecture":"baseline","metrics":{"wallMs":73633,"inputTokens":null,"outputTokens":null,"llmRoundTrips":11,"toolCalls":16,"commandCount":2,"ttfua":{"seconds":5.939,"llmCallsBefore":1,"toolCallsBefore":0},"waste":{"ratio":0.25,"wasted":4,"total":16},"claimedCompletion":true,"finishReason":"session-ended","tests":{"executed":["parse: priority is a non-negative integer in the parsed task","parse: throws on non-numeric priority","parse: throws on negative priority","parse: preserves the task id","scheduler: lower priority number runs first across digit widths","scheduler: ties keep FIFO insertion order","scheduler: mixed priorities with ties","queue: drain does not mutate the queue"],"scores":{"recall":1,"precision":0.875,"executedCount":8,"executedNecessaryCount":7,"necessaryTotal":7,"missedMust":[],"executedIrrelevant":["parse: preserves the task id"],"unmatchedExecuted":[]}},"tokenMetering":"unavailable (v0.1.2 session log has no usage events)"},"falseCompletion":false}
