{"taskId":"t04","killer":false,"architecture":"b","seed":1001,"startedAt":"2026-08-28T18:33:47.220Z","elapsedMs":241583,"timedOut":false,"runError":null,"finishReason":"finish-tool","packet":{"goal_spec":{"goal":"make the repository's test suite pass, conforming to README.md as the authoritative spec","constraints":["only-src","no-new-deps","api-stable","stay-in-workspace"]},"goal_status":{"phase":"branch-search-complete","hypotheses_investigated":3,"selection":"rank confirmed>inconclusive, then evidence count; selected h1 (confirmed, 5 evidence items)"},"selected_hypothesis":"h1: undefined","verified_facts":["src/parse.js returns `{ id: payload.id, priority: trimmed }` where `trimmed = raw.trim()` is a string; no radix-10 conversion or validation exists in the function.","Direct check: `node -e \"import('./src/parse.js')...parseTask({id:'a', priority:' 10 '})\"` printed `{\"id\":\"a\",\"priority\":\"10\"}` with `typeof t.priority === 'string'`, not the number 10.","`node --test`: test/parse.test.js 'parse: priority is a non-negative integer in the parsed task' fails with actual `{ id: 'a', priority: '10' }` vs expected `{ id: 'a', priority: 10 }`.","`node --test`: test/scheduler.test.js 'lower priority number runs first across digit widths' fails with actual `['c','b','a']` vs expected `['c','a','b']` — lexicographic string comparison ('10' < '2') confirming raw strings reach the comparator.","RangeError tests for 'soon' and '-3' also fail (missing expected exception) because parseTask never validates/converts the trimmed string, consistent with the same root cause."],"evidence_refs":["branch-report:h1"],"artifact_refs":["src/parse.js"],"unresolved_questions":["h2: confirmed — parseTask performs no validity check on the trimmed priority content: non-numeric ('soon') and negative ('-3') strings pass straight through, so the required RangeError is never thrown (the only guard is the typeof-string TypeError check).","h3: refuted — The ordering contract is not enforced at the comparison/pipeline boundary: compare() uses `taskA.priority < taskB.priority`, which is lexicographic for strings, and queue.js/scheduler.js feed parseTask's output into it without guaranteeing integer priorities — so the raw string '10' sorts before '2' and the interaction rule (integers must flow to the comparator) is violated."],"recommended_next_action":"Fix the confirmed root cause (src/parse.js) under src/ per the README spec, then run the test suite to verify."},"telemetry":{"branch":{"phases":[{"phase":"enumerate","ms":78616,"hypotheses":3},{"phase":"investigate","ms":124029,"branches":3,"reportsParsed":3},{"phase":"converge+handoff","ms":202645,"selected":"h1","packetBytes":2299}],"packetBytes":2299,"totalMs":202645,"selectionReason":"rank confirmed>inconclusive, then evidence count; selected h1 (confirmed, 5 evidence items)"},"handoff":{"packetBytes":2299,"packetFields":["goal_spec","goal_status","selected_hypothesis","verified_facts","evidence_refs","artifact_refs","unresolved_questions","recommended_next_action"]},"usage":{"inputTokens":98440,"outputTokens":19339,"cachedTokens":75264,"requests":33,"retries":0,"errors":0}},"verify":{"verdict":"PASS","gates":{"bugNotReproducible":{"ok":true,"exitCode":0,"output":"original bug not reproducible\n"},"trunkTestsPass":{"ok":true,"exitCode":0,"counts":{"tests":8,"pass":8,"fail":0},"tail":"TAP version 13\n# Subtest: parse: priority is a non-negative integer in the parsed task\nok 1 - parse: priority is a non-negative integer in the parsed task\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 1.3403\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: parse: throws on non-numeric priority\nok 2 - parse: throws on non-numeric priority\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 0.4029\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: parse: throws on negative priority\nok 3 - parse: throws on negative priority\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 0.0949\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: parse: preserves the task id\nok 4 - parse: preserves the task id\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 0.0674\n  type: 'test'\